{
  "name": "Automated US FDA Recalls & Safety Monitor (Food, Drug & Devices) — Daily B2B Data & Compliance Pipeline",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Automated US FDA Recalls & Safety Monitor (Food, Drug & Devices) Pipeline (Daily B2B M2M Workflow)\n\n**Overview:**\nMonitors and enriches official U.S. FDA enforcement recall reports across Food, Drugs, and Medical Devices via openFDA. Calculates hazard severity scores (0-100) and generates Markdown legal briefs for Product Liability law firms and retail compliance.\n\n**Powered by Apify Actor:** [b2b-quant-apis/us-fda-recalls-safety-monitor](https://apify.com/b2b-quant-apis/us-fda-recalls-safety-monitor)\n\n### Quick Setup (2 Minutes):\n1. Create a free Apify account and copy your personal token from **Settings -> Integrations**.\n2. Open the **Apify Engine: us-fda-recalls-safety-monitor** HTTP Request node and configure a **Header Auth** credential with:\n   - **Name:** `Authorization`\n   - **Value:** `Bearer <YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN_HERE>`\n3. Customize the JSON input payload in the HTTP Request node and set your destination Webhook/Slack URL.\n4. Toggle the workflow **Active** to run automatically every morning at 07:00 AM!",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "48282cef-69f5-517b-b20f-b6a3f54c831c",
      "name": "Setup Instructions & Architecture",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 7 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "4b338778-770a-5dd4-94a8-055bfea56abf",
      "name": "Daily 07:00 AM Schedule Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        220,
        520
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.apify.com/v2/acts/b2b-quant-apis~us-fda-recalls-safety-monitor/run-sync-get-dataset-items",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "{\n  \"drug_names\": [\n    \"ozempic\",\n    \"semaglutide\",\n    \"eliquis\"\n  ],\n  \"include_recalls\": true,\n  \"max_results\": 10\n}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 300000
        }
      },
      "id": "ded04659-69a7-5c52-817d-82c46a88f6f8",
      "name": "Apify Engine: us-fda-recalls-safety-monitor",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        500,
        520
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "aa06f282-8408-5dd3-b212-274b78974052",
              "leftValue": "={{ Object.keys($json).length }}",
              "rightValue": 0,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gt"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        }
      },
      "id": "e71e0b60-0f34-5685-917e-697ed320428b",
      "name": "Validate Structured Dataset Output",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        780,
        520
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.example.com/v1/b2b-compliance-webhook-receiver",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ actor: 'us-fda-recalls-safety-monitor', timestamp: $now, record: $json }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        }
      },
      "id": "ec5b7754-8f08-5570-8345-27e59e4b2df9",
      "name": "Dispatch to Enterprise CRM / Slack Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
